<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Computer Network Basics</title>

    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #eef9ff;
            padding: 30px;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 850px;
            margin: auto;
            background: white;
            padding: 30px;
            border-radius: 18px;
        }

        h1 {
            text-align: center;
            color: #087ea4;
        }

        .network {
            padding: 18px;
            margin: 15px 0;
            background: #e4f7fc;
            border-radius: 12px;
        }

        h2 {
            color: #087ea4;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

<div class="container">

    <h1>🌐 Computer Network Basics</h1>

    <div class="network">
        <h2>What is a Network?</h2>
        <p>
            A computer network connects devices so that they can
            communicate and share information.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="network">
        <h2>LAN</h2>
        <p>
            Local Area Network connects devices within a limited area,
            such as a school or office.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="network">
        <h2>WAN</h2>
        <p>
            Wide Area Network covers a large geographical area.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="network">
        <h2>Router</h2>
        <p>
            A router helps direct data between different networks.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="network">
        <h2>Network Benefits</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>File sharing</li>
            <li>Resource sharing</li>
            <li>Communication</li>
            <li>Internet access</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

</div>

</body>
</html>
